<!-- QLC+ (Horizont HILO lighting show) - RigPilot Device Definition

     RigPilot drives a QLC+ show over MIDI rather than a physical device.

     Scene toggles are wired to Toggle-mode virtual-console buttons: a single
     Note On flips the function on, the next flips it off. They are therefore
     state-dependent (deterministic="false") and emit a Note Off (velocity 0)
     only for MIDI hygiene - QLC+ ignores it for a toggle button.

     Blinders are Flash-mode buttons: they light only while held. They are
     modelled as Hold commands - the Note On (Engage) flashes them on and the
     Note Off (Disengage) releases them, so QLC+ *does* act on both here.

     Note numbering: C-1 = MIDI note 0 (so middle C = C4 = 60).
       Octave -1 (0-11)  : transport / global (Tap Tempo, Blackout)
       Octave  0 (12-23) : blinders (C0 = All, C#0 = Group 1, ...)
       Octave  1 (24-35) : song scene toggles (C1 = Scene 1, ...)          -->
<DeviceDefinition id="qlcplus-horizont-hilo" version="1.0"
                  xmlns="https://rigpilot.app/schemas/device-definition/1">
  <Meta>
    <Manufacturer>QLC+</Manufacturer>
    <Model>Horizont HILO</Model>
    <Author>Flemming Busman</Author>
    <Source>QLC+ MIDI input plugin - project show mapping</Source>
    <Description>Controls a QLC+ lighting show. Set the QLC+ MIDI input profile to the MIDI channel configured in RigPilot's Device Settings. Note numbering uses C-1 = MIDI note 0 (middle C = C4 = 60). Select Song sends a Program Change; pick the song by its number (the label list is 1-based). Scene toggles are state-dependent Toggle buttons (one event on, the next off). Blinders are Flash buttons modelled as Hold commands: they light only while held. Blinder Fade-Time (CC5) is a 0-127 value curve mapped to 0 ms - 5000 ms on the QLC+ side.</Description>
  </Meta>

